Shares of Aditya Birla Sun Life AMC fell over 4% in morning trade on Thursday after the asset manager reported an 8% year-on-year decline in September-quarter net profit amid higher employee costs.
The stock was trading at Rs 912, down Rs 38.40, or 4.04%, at 10:43 am on the NSE.
Net profit fell to Rs 221 crore from Rs 241 crore a year earlier, while revenue rose 5% to Rs 484 crore from Rs 461 crore. Other income declined to Rs 42 crore from Rs 45 crore. Overall expenses increased 20% to Rs 230 crore, with employee benefit expenses jumping 33% to Rs 126 crore.
Nomura maintained its 'Buy' rating but cut its target price to Rs 1,230 from Rs 1,260. Its report was titled "2QFY27 - ESOP cost weighs; flow inflection key" and described the quarter as a "Largely in-line quarter; performance up, marketing on".
Operating profit before tax was Rs 2.5 billion, up 4.2% quarter-on-quarter but 1.3% below estimates. Operating revenue rose 4.9% sequentially to Rs 4.8 billion, beating estimates by 1.4%.
"We now build in INR140mn/quarter ESOP cost (INR80-100mn/quarter from previous ESOP schemes) over FY27-28F," Nomura said, citing the additional cost of the new employee stock option scheme. The brokerage cut its FY27-29 forecast earnings per share by 2-3%, citing lower assets under management growth and higher ESOP and marketing costs.
Motilal Oswal Financial Services reiterated its 'Buy' rating with a target price of Rs 1,160. The brokerage said core operating performance was in line with expectations, while other income drove a 15% beat in reported profit after tax.
Operating expenses rose 21% year-on-year to Rs 2.2 billion, taking the cost-to-income ratio to 44.6% from 38.7%. EBITDA declined 5% to Rs 2.7 billion, with margins falling to 55.4% from 61.3%.
Employee costs rose 33% to Rs 1,263 million, reflecting ESOP expenses, the absence of a prior-year provision reversal and higher headcount. Motilal Oswal identified improvement in flows and market-share recovery as key monitorables, while reiterating its 'Buy' rating and valuing the company at 38 times FY28 estimated core earnings per share.
